<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><fdroid><repo icon="icon.png" name="KabelWacht" pubkey="" timestamp="1785715493" url="https://muelli.github.io/KabelWacht/fdroid/repo" version="20002"><description>Personal F-Droid repository that publishes signed KabelWacht releases, built automatically from tagged commits in CI.</description></repo><application id="com.github.muelli.kabelwacht"><id>com.github.muelli.kabelwacht</id><added>2026-07-31</added><lastupdated>2026-08-02</lastupdated><name>KabelWacht</name><summary>A simple, free WireGuard VPN client: scan, import, and manage tunnels.</summary><desc>KabelWacht is a minimal, fully free-software WireGuard® client for Android.

It does one thing well: manage WireGuard tunnels and connect.

Features:

* Create, list, edit and delete WireGuard profiles.
* Import a configuration by scanning a QR code.
* Import a configuration from a .conf file.
* One-tap connect/disconnect with a per-tunnel switch.
* Userspace WireGuard backend — no root required.

Privacy and freedom:

* 100% free and open-source software (AGPL-3.0-or-later).
* No trackers, no analytics, no advertising.
* No Google Play Services or other proprietary dependencies.
* The only network connection made is your own WireGuard tunnel.

Built on the official WireGuard tunnel library and the ZXing QR decoder.

WireGuard is a registered trademark of Jason A. Donenfeld. This project is not
officially affiliated with or endorsed by the WireGuard project.
